ch(ZZ,CoherentSheaf) -- compute the Chern character of a coherent sheaf
***********************************************************************

  * Function: *note ch: (Schubert2)ch,
  * Usage: 
        ch (i, F)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, that determines a component of
        the Chern character (optional)
      * F, a *note coherent sheaf: (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,, on a complete
        simplicial normal toric variety
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in the intersection
        ring of the underlying variety

Description
===========

Given a locally-free sheaf $E$ of rank $r$ on a smooth variety such that its
Chern class formally factor as chern $E = \prod_{j=1}^r (1 + \alpha_j)$, we
define its Chern character to be ch $E := \sum_{j=1}^r exp(\alpha_j)$. The
$i$-th graded piece of this power series is symmetric in the $\alpha_j$ and,
hence, expressible as a polynomial in the elementary symmetric polynomials in
the $\alpha_j$; we set ch $(i, E)$ to be this polynomial. Because the Chern
character is additive on exact sequences of vector bundles and every coherent
sheaf can be resolved by locally-free sheaves, we can extend this definition to
all coherent sheaves.

The first few components of the Chern character are easily related to other
invariants.

