classGroup(ToricMap) -- make the induced map between class groups
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note classGroup: classGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
  * Usage: 
        classGroup f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, with a smooth target
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, representing the map of abelian
        groups between the corresponding class groups

Description
===========

Given a toric map $f : X \to Y$ where $Y$ a smooth toric variety, this method
returns the induced map of abelian groups from the class group of $Y$ to the
class group of $X$.  For arbitrary normal toric varieties, the *note
classGroup: classGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, is not a functor.  However,
*note classGroup: classGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, is a contravariant
functor on the category of *note smooth: isSmooth_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
normal toric varieties.

We illustrate this method on the projection from the first *note Hirzebruch
surface: hirzebruchSurface_lpZZ_rp, to the *note projective line:
toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp,.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = hirzebruchSurface 1;                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Y = toricProjectiveSpace 1;                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(Y, X, matrix {{1, 0}})                           |
|                                                              |
|o3 = | 1 0 |                                                  |
|                                                              |
|o3 : ToricMap Y <--- X                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f' = classGroup f                                        |
|                                                              |
|o4 = | 1 |                                                    |
|     | 0 |                                                    |
|                                                              |
|              2       1                                       |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert (isWellDefined f and source f' == classGroup Y and|
|         target f' == classGroup X)                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

The induced map between the class groups is compatible with the induced map
between the *note groups of torus-invariant Weil divisors:
weilDivisorGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : f'' = weilDivisorGroup f                             |
|                                                          |
|o6 = | 0 1 |                                              |
|     | 0 0 |                                              |
|     | 1 0 |                                              |
|     | 0 0 |                                              |
|                                                          |
|              4       2                                   |
|o6 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(f' * fromWDivToCl Y  == fromWDivToCl X  * f'')|
+----------------------------------------------------------+

The source of the toric map need not be *note smooth:
isSmooth_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : Z = toricBlowup({0, 1}, X, {1,2});                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert (isWellDefined Z and not isSmooth Z)               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : g = map(Y, Z, matrix{{1, 0}})                            |
|                                                               |
|o10 = | 1 0 |                                                  |
|                                                               |
|o10 : ToricMap Y <--- Z                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : g' = classGroup g                                        |
|                                                               |
|o11 = | 1 |                                                    |
|      | 0 |                                                    |
|      | 0 |                                                    |
|                                                               |
|               3       1                                       |
|o11 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : g'' = weilDivisorGroup g                                 |
|                                                               |
|o12 = | 0 1 |                                                  |
|      | 0 0 |                                                  |
|      | 1 0 |                                                  |
|      | 0 0 |                                                  |
|      | 0 1 |                                                  |
|                                                               |
|               5       2                                       |
|o12 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : assert(g' * fromWDivToCl Y == fromWDivToCl Z  * g'')     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert (isWellDefined g and source g' == classGroup Y and|
|          target g' == classGroup Z)                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note working with toric maps: working with toric maps, -- information
    about toric maps and the induced operations
  * *note classGroup(NormalToricVariety): classGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
    -- make the class group
  * *note weilDivisorGroup(ToricMap): weilDivisorGroup_lpToricMap_rp, -- make
    the induced map between groups of Weil divisors
  * *note picardGroup(ToricMap): picardGroup_lpToricMap_rp, -- make the induced
    map between Picard groups
  * *note pullback(ToricMap,ToricDivisor):
    pullback_lpToricMap_cmToricDivisor_rp, -- make the pullback of a Cartier
    divisor under a toric map

Ways to use this method:
