components(NormalToricVariety) -- list the factors in a product
***************************************************************

  * Function: *note components: (Macaulay2Doc)components,
  * Usage: 
        components X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of the factors from which the
        product was form or just \{X\} if X was not formed by a Cartesian
        product

Description
===========

The Cartesian product of varieties $X_0, X_1, X_2, ...$, all defined over the
same ground field $k$, is the fiber product $X_0 \times_k X_1 \times_k X_2
\times_k ...$.  For normal toric varieties, the fan of the product is given by
the Cartesian product of the underlying fans of the factors.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : X = toricProjectiveSpace 1;|
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : Y = toricProjectiveSpace 2;|
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : Z = toricProjectiveSpace 3;|
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : Seq = (X, Y, Z);           |
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : P = cartesianProduct Seq;  |
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : dim P                      |
|                                |
|o6 = 6                          |
+--------------------------------+
|i7 : assert (dim P == 1+2+3)    |
+--------------------------------+

The factors are cached and can be accessed with *note components:
(Macaulay2Doc)components,.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : factors = components P                                           |
|                                                                      |
|o8 = {X, Y, Z}                                                        |
|                                                                      |
|o8 : List                                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : # factors                                                        |
|                                                                      |
|o9 = 3                                                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert (factors#0 === X and factors#1 === Y and factors#2 === Z)|
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note cartesianProduct(Sequence): cartesianProduct_lpSequence_rp, -- make
    the Cartesian product of normal toric varieties
  * *note NormalToricVariety ** NormalToricVariety: NormalToricVariety _st_st
    NormalToricVariety, -- make the Cartesian product of two normal toric
    varieties
  * *note components: (Macaulay2Doc)components, -- list the components of a
    direct sum

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note components(NormalToricVariety): components_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
    -- list the factors in a product
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

