diagonalToricMap -- make a diagonal map into a Cartesian product
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        diagonalToricMap X
        diagonalToricMap(X,m)
        diagonalToricMap(X,m,A)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, that is positive
      * A, an *note array: (Macaulay2Doc)Array,, whose entries index factors in
        the m-ary product of X
  * Outputs:
      * a *note toric map: ToricMap,, that is a diagonal map from X into the
        m-ary Cartesian product of X with itself; the optional argument A
        indexes factors in the product

Description
===========

Given a positive integer m and a normal toric variety X, the diagonal morphism
is the toric map from X to the m-ary Cartesian product of X such that it
composes to the identity with the i-th *note projection map: NormalToricVariety
^ Array,, for all i in A, and compose to the zero map with the i-th projection
maps for all i not in A.

The most important example arises when m = 2.  For this case, one may omit both
m and A.

