expression(NormalToricVariety) -- get the expression used to format for printing
********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note expression: (Macaulay2Doc)expression,
  * Usage: 
        expression X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Expression,, used to format X for
        printing

Description
===========

This function is primarily called by *note <<: (Macaulay2Doc)printing to a
file, to format printing.  It displays the minimal nonzero lattice points on
each ray and the subsets of rays which determine the maximal cones in the fan.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : toricProjectiveSpace 3                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = normalToricVariety ({{-1, -1, -1}, {1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 1}},    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : NormalToricVariety                                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{{0, 1, 2}, {0, 1, 3}, {0, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}})                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : expression toricProjectiveSpace 3                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = normalToricVariety ({{-1, -1, -1}, {1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 1}},    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Expression of class Adjacent                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{{0, 1, 2}, {0, 1, 3}, {0, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}})                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : rays toricProjectiveSpace 3                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{-1, -1, -1}, {1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 1}}                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : max toricProjectiveSpace 3                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {{0, 1, 2}, {0, 1, 3}, {0, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}}                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : hirzebruchSurface 7                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = normalToricVariety ({{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, 7}, {0, -1}}, {{0, 1}, {0, 3},|
|                                                                             |
|o5 : NormalToricVariety                                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{1, 2}, {2, 3}})                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : expression hirzebruchSurface 7                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = normalToricVariety ({{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, 7}, {0, -1}}, {{0, 1}, {0, 3},|
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Expression of class Adjacent                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{1, 2}, {2, 3}})                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : rays hirzebruchSurface 7                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, 7}, {0, -1}}                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : max hirzebruchSurface 7                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = {{0, 1}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

After assignment to a global variable Macaulay2 knows the toric variety's name,
and this name is used when printing.

+---------------------------------+
|i9 : PP2 = toricProjectiveSpace 3|
|                                 |
|o9 = PP2                         |
|                                 |
|o9 : NormalToricVariety          |
+---------------------------------+
|i10 : expression PP2             |
|                                 |
|o10 = PP2                        |
|                                 |
|o10 : Expression of class Holder |
+---------------------------------+
|i11 : FF7 = hirzebruchSurface 7  |
|                                 |
|o11 = FF7                        |
|                                 |
|o11 : NormalToricVariety         |
+---------------------------------+
|i12 : expression FF7             |
|                                 |
|o12 = FF7                        |
|                                 |
|o12 : Expression of class Holder |
+---------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note finding attributes and properties: finding attributes and properties,
    -- information about accessing features of a normal toric variety
  * *note rays(NormalToricVariety): rays_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    rays of the associated fan
  * *note max(NormalToricVariety): max_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    maximal cones in the associated fan

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note expression(NormalToricVariety): expression_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
    -- get the expression used to format for printing
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

