finding attributes and properties -- information about accessing features of a normal toric variety
***************************************************************************************************

Having made a *note NormalToricVariety: NormalToricVariety,, one can access its
basic invariants or test for some elementary properties by using the following
methods:

Determining attributes and properties of normal toric varieties
===============================================================

  * *note rays(NormalToricVariety): rays_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    rays of the associated fan
  * *note max(NormalToricVariety): max_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    maximal cones in the associated fan
  * *note expression(NormalToricVariety): expression_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
    -- get the expression used to format for printing
  * *note dim(NormalToricVariety): dim_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    dimension of a normal toric variety
  * *note orbits(NormalToricVariety,ZZ): orbits_lpNormalToricVariety_cmZZ_rp,
    -- get a list of the torus orbits (a.k.a. cones in the fan) of a given
    dimension
  * *note isDegenerate(NormalToricVariety):
    isDegenerate_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- whether a toric variety is
    degenerate
  * *note isSimplicial(NormalToricVariety):
    isSimplicial_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- whether a normal toric variety is
    simplicial
  * *note isSmooth(NormalToricVariety): isSmooth_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, --
    whether a normal toric variety is smooth
  * *note isComplete(NormalToricVariety): isComplete_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
    -- whether a toric variety is complete
  * *note isProjective(NormalToricVariety):
    isProjective_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- whether a toric variety is
    projective
  * *note isFano(NormalToricVariety): isFano_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, --
    whether a normal toric variety is Fano
  * *note fan(NormalToricVariety): fan_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the
    'Polyhedra' fan associated to the normal toric variety

See also
========

  * *note making normal toric varieties: making normal toric varieties, --
    information about the basic constructors
  * *note resolving singularities: resolving singularities, -- information
    about find a smooth proper birational surjection
  * *note working with toric maps: working with toric maps, -- information
    about toric maps and the induced operations
  * *note working with divisors: working with divisors, -- information about
    toric divisors and their related groups
  * *note working with sheaves: working with sheaves, -- information about
    coherent sheaves and total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
