hilbertPolynomial(NormalToricVariety) -- compute the multivariate Hilbert polynomial
************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertPolynomial: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertPolynomial,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertPolynomial X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, that is smooth
        and complete
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertPolynomial_lp_pd_pd_pd_
        cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value true, unused
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Hilbert
        polynomial of X

Description
===========

The Hilbert polynomial of a smooth projective toric variety $X$ is the Euler
characteristic of $OO_X(i_0,i_1,...,i_r)$ where $r$ is the rank of the Picard
group of $X$ and $i_0,i_1,...,i_r$ are formal variables.  The Hilbert
polynomial agrees with the Hilbert function when evaluated at any point in the
nef cone.

On projective space, one recovers the standard Hilbert polynomial.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : PP2 = toricProjectiveSpace 2;                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : h0 = hilbertPolynomial PP2                            |
|                                                           |
|     1 2   3                                               |
|o2 = -i  + -i  + 1                                         |
|     2 0   2 0                                             |
|                                                           |
|o2 : QQ[i ]                                                |
|         0                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : factor h0                                             |
|                                                           |
|                      1                                    |
|o3 = (i  + 1)(i  + 2)(-)                                   |
|       0       0      2                                    |
|                                                           |
|o3 : Expression of class Product                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : h1 = hilbertPolynomial (ring PP2, Projective => false)|
|                                                           |
|     1 2   3                                               |
|o4 = -i  + -i + 1                                          |
|     2     2                                               |
|                                                           |
|o4 : QQ[i]                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert (h0 === sub(h1, (ring h1)_0 => (ring h0)_0))   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : PP3 = toricProjectiveSpace 3;                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : h2 = hilbertPolynomial PP3                            |
|                                                           |
|     1 3    2   11                                         |
|o7 = -i  + i  + --i  + 1                                   |
|     6 0    0    6 0                                       |
|                                                           |
|o7 : QQ[i ]                                                |
|         0                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : factor h2                                             |
|                                                           |
|                              1                            |
|o8 = (i  + 1)(i  + 2)(i  + 3)(-)                           |
|       0       0       0      6                            |
|                                                           |
|o8 : Expression of class Product                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : h3 = hilbertPolynomial (ring PP3, Projective => false)|
|                                                           |
|     1 3    2   11                                         |
|o9 = -i  + i  + --i + 1                                    |
|     6           6                                         |
|                                                           |
|o9 : QQ[i]                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert (h2 === sub(h3, (ring h3)_0 => (ring h2)_0))  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

The Hilbert polynomial of a product of normal toric varieties is simply the
product of the Hilbert polynomials of the factors.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : X = toricProjectiveSpace (2) ** toricProjectiveSpace (3);              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : h3 = hilbertPolynomial X                                               |
|                                                                             |
|       1 2 3   1 2 2   1   3   11 2     3   2   1 3   1 2   11        2   3  |
|o12 = --i i  + -i i  + -i i  + --i i  + -i i  + -i  + -i  + --i i  + i  + -i |
|      12 0 1   2 0 1   4 0 1   12 0 1   2 0 1   6 1   2 0    4 0 1    1   2 0|
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        11                                                                   |
|      + --i  + 1                                                             |
|         6 1                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o12 : QQ[i ..i ]                                                             |
|          0   1                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : factor h3                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|                                                1                            |
|o13 = (i  + 1)(i  + 2)(i  + 3)(i  + 1)(i  + 2)(--)                           |
|        1       1       1       0       0      12                            |
|                                                                             |
|o13 : Expression of class Product                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Example 2.9 in [Diane Maclagan and Gregory G. Smith, Uniform bounds on
multigraded regularity (see http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AC/0305215 ), J.
Algebraic Geom. 14 (2005), 137-164] describes the Hilbert polynomials on a
Hirzebruch surface.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : a = random (9)                                                  |
|                                                                      |
|o14 = 8                                                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : FFa = hirzebruchSurface a;                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : h4 = hilbertPolynomial FFa                                      |
|                                                                      |
|               2                                                      |
|o16 = i i  + 4i  + i  + 5i  + 1                                       |
|       0 1     1    0     1                                           |
|                                                                      |
|o16 : QQ[i ..i ]                                                      |
|          0   1                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : R = ring h4;                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : assert (h4 == R_0 * R_1 + (a/2)*R_1^2 + R_0 + ((a+2)/2)*R_1 + 1)|
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

The Hilbert polynomial is computed using the Hirzebruch-Riemann-Roch Theorem.
In particular, this method depends on the *note Schubert2: (Schubert2)Top,
package.

See also
========

  * *note working with sheaves: working with sheaves, -- information about
    coherent sheaves and total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
  * *note hilbertPolynomial(NormalToricVariety,CoherentSheaf):
    hilbertPolynomial_lpNormalToricVariety_cmCoherentSheaf_rp, -- compute the
    multivariate Hilbert polynomial
  * *note isSmooth(NormalToricVariety): isSmooth_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, --
    whether a normal toric variety is smooth

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note hilbertPolynomial(NormalToricVariety):
    hilbertPolynomial_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- compute the multivariate
    Hilbert polynomial
  * "hilbertPolynomial(NormalToricVariety,Ring)"
  * "hilbertPolynomial(NormalToricVariety,SheafOfRings)"
