hilbertPolynomial(NormalToricVariety,CoherentSheaf) -- compute the multivariate Hilbert polynomial
**************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertPolynomial: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertPolynomial,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertPolynomial (X, F)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, that is smooth
        and complete
      * F, a *note coherent sheaf: (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,, on X
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertPolynomial_lp_pd_pd_pd_
        cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value true, unused
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Hilbert
        polynomial of X

Description
===========

The Hilbert polynomial of a coherent sheaf $F$ on smooth normal toric variety
$X$ is the Euler characteristic of $F ** OO_X(i_0,i_1,...,i_r)$ where $r$ is
the rank of the Picard group of $X$ and $i_0,i_1,...,i_r$ are formal variables.
The Hilbert polynomial agrees with the Hilbert function when evaluated at any
point sufficiently far in the interior of in the nef cone.

For a graded module over the total coordinate ring of $X$, this method computes
the Hilbert polynomial of the corresponding coherent sheaf.  Given an ideal $I$
in the total coordinate ring, it computes the Hilbert polynomial of the
coherent sheaf associated to $S^1/I$.

The cotangent bundle on a smooth surface provides simple examples.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : PP2 = toricProjectiveSpace 2;                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : OmegaPP2 = cotangentSheaf PP2                       |
|                                                         |
|o2 = cokernel {2} | x_2  |                               |
|              {2} | x_0  |                               |
|              {2} | -x_1 |                               |
|                                                         |
|                                             3           |
|o2 : coherent sheaf on PP2, quotient of OO    (-2)       |
|                                          PP2            |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h0 = hilbertPolynomial (PP2, OmegaPP2)              |
|                                                         |
|      2                                                  |
|o3 = i  - 1                                              |
|      0                                                  |
|                                                         |
|o3 : QQ[i ]                                              |
|         0                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : for i to 10 list hilbertFunction(i, module OmegaPP2)|
|                                                         |
|o4 = {0, 0, 3, 8, 15, 24, 35, 48, 63, 80, 99}            |
|                                                         |
|o4 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = ring h0;                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : for i to 10 list sub(h0, R_0 => i)                  |
|                                                         |
|o6 = {-1, 0, 3, 8, 15, 24, 35, 48, 63, 80, 99}           |
|                                                         |
|o6 : List                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : FF3 = hirzebruchSurface 3;                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : OmegaFF3 = cotangentSheaf FF3                                         |
|                                                                           |
|o8 = cokernel {2, 0}  | 3x_1x_3 |                                          |
|              {-2, 2} | x_0     |                                          |
|              {-2, 2} | -x_2    |                                          |
