hirzebruchSurface(ZZ) -- make any Hirzebruch surface
****************************************************

  * Function: *note hirzebruchSurface: hirzebruchSurface_lpZZ_rp,
  * Usage: 
        hirzebruchSurface a
  * Inputs:
      * a, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, that determines which
        Hirzebruch surface
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ,
        that specifies the coefficient ring of the *note total coordinate ring:
        ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
      * Variable => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value x,
        that specifies the *note base name: (Macaulay2Doc)baseName, for the
        indexed variables in the total coordinate ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, that is a Hirzebruch
        surface

Description
===========

The $a$-{th} Hirzebruch surface is a smooth projective normal toric variety.
It can be defined as the $\PP^1$-bundle over $X = \PP^1$ associated to the
sheaf ${\mathcal O}_X(0) \oplus {\mathcal O}_X(a)$.  It is also the quotient of
affine $4$-space by a rank two torus.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : FF3 = hirzebruchSurface 3;                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : rays FF3                                                        |
|                                                                     |
|o2 = {{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, 3}, {0, -1}}                              |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : max FF3                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = {{0, 1}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}                                |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : dim FF3                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o4 = 2                                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : ring FF3                                                        |
|                                                                     |
|o5 = QQ[x ..x ]                                                      |
|         0   3                                                       |
|                                                                     |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : degrees ring FF3                                                |
|                                                                     |
|o6 = {{1, 0}, {-3, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}}                               |
|                                                                     |
|o6 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : ideal FF3                                                       |
|                                                                     |
|o7 = ideal (x x , x x , x x , x x )                                  |
|             2 3   1 2   0 3   0 1                                   |
|                                                                     |
|o7 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                                             |
|                  0   3                                              |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert (isWellDefined FF3 and isProjective FF3 and isSmooth FF3)|
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

When $a = 0$, we obtain $\PP^1 \times \PP^1$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : FF0 = hirzebruchSurface (0, CoefficientRing => ZZ/32003, Variable => y);|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : rays FF0                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = {{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, 0}, {0, -1}}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : max FF0                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = {{0, 1}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : ring FF0                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|        ZZ                                                                   |
|o12 = -----[y ..y ]                                                          |
|      32003  0   3                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o12 : PolynomialRing                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : degrees ring FF0                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = {{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}}                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o13 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : I = ideal FF0                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o14 = ideal (y y , y y , y y , y y )                                         |
|              2 3   1 2   0 3   0 1                                          |
|                                                                             |
|                 ZZ                                                          |
|o14 : Ideal of -----[y ..y ]                                                 |
|               32003  0   3                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : decompose I                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o15 = {ideal (y , y ), ideal (y , y )}                                       |
|               2   0           3   1                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o15 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : assert (isWellDefined FF0 and isProjective FF3 and isSmooth FF3)       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The map from the *note group of torus-invariant Weil divisors:
weilDivisorGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, to the *note class group:
classGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, is chosen so that the positive orthant
corresponds to the cone of nef line bundles.

+------------------------+
|i17 : nefGenerators FF3 |
|                        |
|o17 = | 1 0 |           |
|      | 0 1 |           |
|                        |
|               2       2|
|o17 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ |
+------------------------+
|i18 : nefGenerators FF0 |
|                        |
|o18 = | 1 0 |           |
|      | 0 1 |           |
|                        |
|               2       2|
|o18 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ |
+------------------------+

