inducedMap(ToricMap) -- make the induced map between total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
**********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note inducedMap: (Macaulay2Doc)inducedMap,
  * Usage: 
        inducedMap f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, with a smooth target
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)inducedMap_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value null, unused
      * *note Verify: (Macaulay2Doc)inducedMap_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerify=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value true, unused
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, between the total homogeneous
        coordinate rings (aka Cox rings)

Description
===========

Any morphism of varieties whose target is a smooth normal toric variety is
determined by a collection of lines bundles together with a section of each
line bundle.  This data defines a ring map whose source is the *note total
coordinate ring: ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, (a.k.a. Cox ring) of target
variety.  For more information, see David A. Cox, "The Functor of a Smooth
Toric Variety", The Tohoku Mathematical Journal, Second Series, 47 (1995)
251-262, arXiv:alg-geom/9312001v2 (see https://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9312001
).

Given a toric map $f : X \to Y$ where $Y$ is smooth, this method returns the
induced map from the total coordinate ring $S$ of $Y$ to the total coordinate
ring $R$ of $X$.  Since $f$ is torus-equivariant, each variable in the
polynomial ring $S$ maps to a monomial in $R$.

As a first example, we compute the map on the total coordinate rings induced by
the natural inclusion of the *note affine plane: affineSpace_lpZZ_rp, into
*note projective plane: toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp,.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = affineSpace 2;                            |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = toricProjectiveSpace 2;                   |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(P, A, 1)                              |
|                                                   |
|o3 = | 1 0 |                                       |
|     | 0 1 |                                       |
|                                                   |
|o3 : ToricMap P <--- A                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (R = ring A, S = ring P);                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f' = inducedMap f                             |
|                                                   |
|o5 = map (R, S, {1, x , x })                       |
|                     0   1                         |
|                                                   |
|o5 : RingMap R <-- S                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : f' vars S                                     |
|                                                   |
|o6 = | 1 x_0 x_1 |                                 |
|                                                   |
|             1      3                              |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : ideal f == 0                                  |
|                                                   |
|o7 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : degrees source f'                             |
|                                                   |
|o8 = {{1}, {1}, {1}}                               |
|                                                   |
|o8 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : degrees target f'                             |
|                                                   |
|o9 = {{}, {}}                                      |
|                                                   |
|o9 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert (isWellDefined f and isHomogeneous f')|
+---------------------------------------------------+

The second example considers the projection from the third *note Hirzebruch
surface: hirzebruchSurface_lpZZ_rp, to the *note projective line:
toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp,.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : X = hirzebruchSurface 3;                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : Y = toricProjectiveSpace 1;                  |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : g = map(Y, X, matrix {{1, 0}})               |
|                                                   |
|o13 = | 1 0 |                                      |
|                                                   |
|o13 : ToricMap Y <--- X                            |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : (R = ring Y, S = ring X);                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : g' = inducedMap g                            |
|                                                   |
|o15 = map (S, R, {x , x })                         |
|                   2   0                           |
|                                                   |
|o15 : RingMap S <-- R                              |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : degrees source g'                            |
|                                                   |
|o16 = {{1}, {1}}                                   |
|                                                   |
|o16 : List                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : degrees target g'                            |
|                                                   |
|o17 = {{1, 0}, {-3, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}}            |
|                                                   |
|o17 : List                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : assert (isWellDefined g and isHomogeneous g')|
+---------------------------------------------------+

In the third example, we consider a third Veronese embedding of the projective
line into projective $3$-space.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i19 : Z = toricProjectiveSpace 3;                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i20 : h = map(Z, Y, matrix {{1}, {2}, {3}})                              |
|                                                                         |
|o20 = | 1 |                                                              |
|      | 2 |                                                              |
|      | 3 |                                                              |
|                                                                         |
|o20 : ToricMap Z <--- Y                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i21 : (R = ring Y, S = ring X);                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i22 : h' = inducedMap h                                                  |
|                                                                         |
|                            3   2       2   3                            |
|o22 = map (R, QQ[x ..x ], {x , x x , x x , x })                          |
|                  0   3     0   0 1   0 1   1                            |
|                                                                         |
|o22 : RingMap R <-- QQ[x ..x ]                                           |
|                        0   3                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i23 : degrees source g'                                                  |
|                                                                         |
|o23 = {{1}, {1}}                                                         |
|                                                                         |
|o23 : List                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i24 : degrees target g'                                                  |
|                                                                         |
|o24 = {{1, 0}, {-3, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}}                                  |
|                                                                         |
|o24 : List                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i25 : ideal h                                                            |
|                                                                         |
|              2                       2                                  |
|o25 = ideal (x  - x x , x x  - x x , x  - x x )                          |
|              2    1 3   1 2    0 3   1    0 2                           |
|                                                                         |
|o25 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                                                |
|                   0   3                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i26 : assert (isWellDefined h and isHomogeneous h' and ideal h == ker h')|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

To ensure that the induced map is homogeneous, the optional argument *note
DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)DegreeMap, is used to record the degree of the
monomials in the target ring $R$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i27 : code (inducedMap, ToricMap)                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o27 = -- code for method: inducedMap(ToricMap)                               |
|      ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/NormalToricVarieties/ToricMaps.m2:394|
|      :34-404:5: --source code:                                              |
|      inducedMap ToricMap := RingMap => o -> (cacheValue symbol inducedMap) (|
|              Y := target f;                                                 |
|              S := ring Y;                                                   |
|              R := ring source f;                                            |
|              m := picardGroup f; -- degree map                              |
|              map(R, S, apply(numgens S, i -> (                              |
|                          exps := entries pullback(f, Y_i);                  |
|                          product(numgens R, j -> R_j^(exps#j)))),           |
|                  DegreeMap => (deg -> first entries (matrix{deg} * transpose|
|              )                                                              |
|          )                                                                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|f -> (                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
| m)))                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This method assumes that the target is smooth. One may verify this by using
*note isSmooth(NormalToricVariety): isSmooth_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,.

