isDegenerate(NormalToricVariety) -- whether a toric variety is degenerate
*************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isDegenerate: isDegenerate_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
  * Usage: 
        isDegenerate X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if the fan of X is contained in a proper linear
        subspace of its ambient space

Description
===========

A $d$-dimensional normal toric variety is degenerate if its rays do not span
$\QQ^d$.  For example, projective spaces and Hirzebruch surfaces are not
degenerate.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : assert not isDegenerate toricProjectiveSpace 3|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : assert not isDegenerate hirzebruchSurface 7   |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Although one typically works with non-degenerate toric varieties, not all
normal toric varieties are non-degenerate.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : U = normalToricVariety ({{4,-1,0},{0,1,0}},{{0,1}});|
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isDegenerate U                                      |
|                                                         |
|o4 = true                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Many routines in this package, such as the *note total coordinate ring:
ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,, require the normal toric variety to be
non-degenerate.

See also
========

  * *note finding attributes and properties: finding attributes and properties,
    -- information about accessing features of a normal toric variety
  * *note rays(NormalToricVariety): rays_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    rays of the associated fan

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isDegenerate(NormalToricVariety):
    isDegenerate_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- whether a toric variety is
    degenerate
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

