isDominant(ToricMap) -- whether a toric map is dominant
*******************************************************

  * Function: *note isDominant: isDominant_lpToricMap_rp,
  * Usage: 
        isDominant f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if the image is dense

Description
===========

A morphism of varieties is dominant if the image is dense. For a toric map, it
suffices to check that the dimension of the image is the dimension of the
target.

We demonstrate that the natural inclusion from the *note affine plane:
affineSpace_lpZZ_rp, into the *note projective plane:
toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp, is a dominant, but not surjective

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = affineSpace 2;                                              |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = toricProjectiveSpace 2;                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(P, A, 1)                                                |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = | 1 0 |                                                         |
|     | 0 1 |                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : ToricMap P <--- A                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isDominant f                                                    |
|                                                                     |
|o4 = true                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isSurjective f                                                  |
|                                                                     |
|o5 = false                                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert (isWellDefined f and isDominant f and not isSurjective f)|
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

A toric map from the projective line to the projective plane is not dominant.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : X = toricProjectiveSpace 1;                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : g = map(P, X, matrix{{2}, {1}})                                 |
|                                                                     |
|o8 = | 2 |                                                           |
|     | 1 |                                                           |
|                                                                     |
|o8 : ToricMap P <--- X                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isDominant g                                                    |
|                                                                     |
|o9 = false                                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : I = ideal g                                                    |
|                                                                     |
|                    2                                                |
|o10 = ideal(x x  - x )                                               |
|             0 1    2                                                |
|                                                                     |
|o10 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                                            |
|                   0   2                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : assert (isWellDefined g and not isDominant g and codim I === 1)|
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

To avoid repeating a computation, the package caches the result in the *note
CacheTable: (Macaulay2Doc)CacheTable, of the toric map.

See also
========

  * *note working with toric maps: working with toric maps, -- information
    about toric maps and the induced operations
  * *note map(NormalToricVariety,NormalToricVariety,Matrix):
    map_lpNormalToricVariety_cmNormalToricVariety_cmMatrix_rp, -- make a
    torus-equivariant map between normal toric varieties
  * *note map(NormalToricVariety,NormalToricVariety,ZZ):
    map_lpNormalToricVariety_cmNormalToricVariety_cmZZ_rp, -- make a
    torus-equivariant map between normal toric varieties
  * *note isComplete(NormalToricVariety): isComplete_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
    -- whether a toric variety is complete

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isDominant(ToricMap): isDominant_lpToricMap_rp, -- whether a toric
    map is dominant
