isNef(ToricDivisor) -- whether a torus-invariant Weil divisor is nef
********************************************************************

  * Function: *note isNef: isNef_lpToricDivisor_rp,
  * Usage: 
        isNef D
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note toric divisor: ToricDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if the divisor is nef

Description
===========

A $\QQ$-Cartier divisor is nef (short for numerically effective or numerically
eventually free) if the intersection product of the divisor with every complete
irreducible curve is nonnegative.  The definition depends only on the numerical
equivalence class of the divisor.  For a torus-invariant $\QQ$-Cartier divisor
on a complete normal toric variety, the following are equivalent:

  * the divisor is nef;
  * some positive integer multiply of the divisor is Cartier and basepoint
    free;
  * the real piecewise linear support function associated to the divisor is
    convex.

A torus-invariant Cartier divisor is nef if and only if it is basepoint free;
in other words, the associated line bundle is generated by its global sections.

On a Hirzebruch surface, three of the four torus-invariant irreducible divisors
are nef, and none are ample.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X1 = hirzebruchSurface 2;               |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : assert (isNef X1_0 and not isAmple X1_0)|
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert not isNef X1_1                   |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert (isNef X1_2 and not isAmple X1_2)|
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert (isNef X1_3 and not isAmple X1_3)|
+---------------------------------------------+

Not every $\QQ$-Cartier nef divisor is basepoint free.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : X2 = weightedProjectiveSpace {2,3,5};                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : D = X2_1 - X2_0                                           |
|                                                               |
|o7 = - X2  + X2                                                |
|         0     1                                               |
|                                                               |
|o7 : ToricDivisor on X2                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert (isNef D and HH^0(X2, OO D) == 0)                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert all (dim X2, i -> HH^i(X2, OO D) == 0)             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert not isCartier D                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : assert isCartier (30*D)                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : HH^0 (X2, OO (30*D))                                     |
|                                                               |
|        21                                                     |
|o12 = QQ                                                       |
|                                                               |
|o12 : QQ-module, free                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : assert all (dim X2 -1, i -> HH^(i+1)(X2, OO (30*D)) == 0)|
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

There are smooth complete normal toric varieties with no nontrivial nef
divisors.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : X3 = normalToricVariety({{1,0,0},{0,1,0},{0,0,1},{0,-1,2},{0,0,-1},{-1,|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|1,-1},{-1,0,-1},{-1,-1,0}},{{0,1,2},{0,2,3},{0,3,4},{0,4,5},{0,1,5},{1,2,7},{|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|2,3,7},{3,4,7},{4,5,6},{4,6,7},{5,6,7},{1,5,7}});                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : assert (isComplete X3 and not isProjective X3)                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : assert not any (#rays X3, i -> isNef X3_i)                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : assert isNef (0*X3_1)                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : assert (nefGenerators X3 == 0)                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The most basic vanishing theorem for normal toric varieties states that the
higher cohomology of coherent sheaf associated to a nef divisor is zero.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i19 : X4 = kleinschmidt (9,{1,2,3});                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i20 : assert (isNef X4_0 and not isAmple X4_0)                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i21 : assert all (dim X4 - 1, i -> HH^(i+1)(X4, OO X4_0) == 0)|
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i22 : D = X4_0 + X4_4                                         |
|                                                              |
|o22 = X4  + X4                                                |
|        0     4                                               |
|                                                              |
|o22 : ToricDivisor on X4                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i23 : assert (isNef D and isAmple D)                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i24 : assert all (dim X4 - 1, i -> HH^(i+1)(X4, OO D) == 0)   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note working with divisors: working with divisors, -- information about
    toric divisors and their related groups
  * *note nefGenerators(NormalToricVariety):
    nefGenerators_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- compute generators of the nef
    cone
  * *note isComplete(NormalToricVariety): isComplete_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
    -- whether a toric variety is complete
  * *note kleinschmidt(ZZ,List): kleinschmidt_lpZZ_cmList_rp, -- make any
    smooth normal toric variety having Picard rank two
  * *note isQQCartier(ToricDivisor): isQQCartier_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether
    a torus-invariant Weil divisor is QQ-Cartier
  * *note isAmple(ToricDivisor): isAmple_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether a
    torus-invariant Weil divisor is ample

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isNef(ToricDivisor): isNef_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether a
    torus-invariant Weil divisor is nef
