isWellDefined(ToricDivisor) -- whether a toric divisor is well-defined
**********************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        isWellDefined D
  * Inputs:
      * D, a *note toric divisor: ToricDivisor,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if underlying data structure is correctly formatted

Description
===========

This function checks that the following aspects of the data structure:

  * the underlying *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, has the expected
    keys, namely the integers from 0 to n-1 where n = # rays variety D,
    variety, and cache,
  * the value of each integer key is an *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
  * the value of the variety key is a *note NormalToricVariety:
    NormalToricVariety,,
  * the value of the cache key is a *note CacheTable:
    (Macaulay2Doc)CacheTable,.
+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : PP2 = toricProjectiveSpace 2     |
|                                      |
|o1 = PP2                              |
|                                      |
|o1 : NormalToricVariety               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : D1 = toricDivisor ({2,-7,3}, PP2)|
|                                      |
|o2 = 2*PP2  - 7*PP2  + 3*PP2          |
|          0        1        2         |
|                                      |
|o2 : ToricDivisor on PP2              |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert isWellDefined D1          |
+--------------------------------------+
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : debugLevel = 1;                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D2 = new ToricDivisor from hashTable { 0 => 2, symbol variety => PP2,   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : ToricDivisor on PP2                                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|symbol cache => new CacheTable};                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert not isWellDefined D2                                             |
|-- missing key(s): {1, 2}                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : D3 = new ToricDivisor from hashTable { 0 => 2, 1 => x, 2 => 3, symbol   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : ToricDivisor on PP2                                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|variety => PP2, symbol cache => new CacheTable};                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert not isWellDefined D3                                             |
|expected 1-th coefficient to be an integer                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : D4 = new ToricDivisor from hashTable { 0 => 2, 1 => -7, 2 => 3, symbol  |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : ToricDivisor on 7                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|variety => 7, symbol cache => new CacheTable};                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert not isWellDefined D4                                            |
|expected a divisor over a normal toric variety                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The function *note expression(ToricDivisor): expression_lpToricDivisor_rp,
assumes that the input toric divisor is well-defined.

