makeSimplicial(NormalToricVariety) -- make a birational simplicial toric variety
********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note makeSimplicial: makeSimplicial_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
  * Usage: 
        makeSimplicial X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0,
        either 0 or 1
  * Outputs:
      * a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, that is simplicial

Description
===========

A normal toric variety is simplicial if every cone in its fan is simplicial and
a cone is simplicial if its minimal generators are linearly independent over
$\QQ$.  In fact, the following conditions on a normal toric variety $X$ are
equivalent:

  * X is simplicial;
  * every Weil divisor on X has a positive integer multiple that is Cartier;
  * the Picard group of X has finite index in the class group of X;
  * X has only finite quotient singularities.

For more information, see Proposition 4.2.7 in Cox-Little-Schenck's Toric
Varieties.

Given a normal toric variety, this method makes a simplicial toric variety with
the same rays by triangulating the non-simplicial maximal cones.  For the 0
strategy, the triangulation is constructed by repeated regular subdivisions
using random integral weight vectors.  For the 1 strategy, the triangulation is
constructed by repeated pushing subdivisions (i.e. toricBlowups at a given
ray).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = normalToricVariety (id_(ZZ^3) | - id_(ZZ^3));                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : assert not isSimplicial X                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Y1 = makeSimplicial X;                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert isSimplicial Y1                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert (rays Y1 === rays X)                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : max Y1                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {{0, 1, 3}, {0, 1, 5}, {0, 2, 3}, {0, 2, 6}, {0, 4, 5}, {0, 4, 6}, {1,  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     3, 7}, {1, 5, 7}, {2, 3, 7}, {2, 6, 7}, {4, 5, 7}, {4, 6, 7}}           |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : max X                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {{0, 1, 2, 3}, {0, 1, 4, 5}, {0, 2, 4, 6}, {1, 3, 5, 7}, {2, 3, 6, 7},  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {4, 5, 6, 7}}                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : Y2 = makeSimplicial(X, Strategy => 1);                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert isSimplicial Y2                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert (rays Y2 === rays X)                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : max Y2                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = {{0, 1, 3}, {0, 1, 5}, {0, 2, 3}, {0, 2, 6}, {0, 4, 5}, {0, 4, 6}, {1, |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      3, 7}, {1, 5, 7}, {2, 3, 7}, {2, 6, 7}, {4, 5, 7}, {4, 6, 7}}          |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : max Y1 == max Y2                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = true                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If the initial toric variety is simplicial, then this method simply returns it.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : PP3 = toricProjectiveSpace 3;                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert isSimplicial PP3                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : Z = makeSimplicial PP3;                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : assert (rays Z === rays PP3 and max Z === max PP3)|
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note resolving singularities: resolving singularities, -- information
    about find a smooth proper birational surjection
  * *note isSimplicial(NormalToricVariety):
    isSimplicial_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- whether a normal toric variety is
    simplicial

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note makeSimplicial(NormalToricVariety):
    makeSimplicial_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make a birational simplicial
    toric variety
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

