making normal toric varieties -- information about the basic constructors
*************************************************************************

A normal toric variety corresponds to a strongly convex rational polyhedral fan
in affine space.  In this package, the fan associated to a normal
$d$-dimensional toric variety lies in the rational vector space $\QQ^d$ with
underlying lattice $N = \ZZ^d$. The fan is encoded by the minimal nonzero
lattice points on its rays and the set of rays defining the maximal cones (a
maximal cone is not properly contained in another cone in the fan).  More
information about the correspondence between normal toric varieties and
strongly convex rational polyhedral fans appears in Subsection 3.1 of
Cox-Little-Schenck.

The general method for creating *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,
is *note normalToricVariety: normalToricVariety_lpList_cmList_rp,.  However,
there are many additional methods for constructing other specific types of
normal toric varieties.

Constructors for normal toric varieties
=======================================

  * *note normalToricVariety(List,List): normalToricVariety_lpList_cmList_rp,
    -- make a normal toric variety
  * *note normalToricVariety(Matrix): normalToricVariety_lpMatrix_rp, -- make a
