max(NormalToricVariety) -- get the maximal cones in the associated fan
**********************************************************************

  * Function: *note max: (Macaulay2Doc)max,
  * Usage: 
        max X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of lists of nonnegative integers;
        each entry indexes the rays that generate a maximal cone in the fan

Description
===========

A normal toric variety corresponds to a strongly convex rational polyhedral fan
in affine space.  In this package, the fan associated to a normal
$d$-dimensional toric variety lies in the rational vector space $\QQ^d$ with
underlying lattice $N = \ZZ^d$. The fan is encoded by the minimal nonzero
lattice points on its rays and the set of rays defining the maximal cones
(where a maximal cone is not properly contained in another cone in the fan).
The rays are ordered and indexed by nonnegative integers: $0, 1, \dots, n-1$.
Using this indexing, a maximal cone in the fan corresponds to a sublist of $\{
0, 1, \dots, n-1 \}$; the entries index the rays that generate the cone.

The examples show the maximal cones for the projective line, *note projective
$3$-space: toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp,, a *note Hirzebruch surface:
hirzebruchSurface_lpZZ_rp,, and a *note weighted projective space:
weightedProjectiveSpace_lpList_rp,.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : PP1 = toricProjectiveSpace 1;|
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : # rays PP1                   |
|                                  |
|o2 = 2                            |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : max PP1                      |
|                                  |
|o3 = {{0}, {1}}                   |
|                                  |
|o3 : List                         |
+----------------------------------+
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : PP3 = toricProjectiveSpace 3;               |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : # rays PP3                                  |
|                                                 |
|o5 = 4                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : max PP3                                     |
|                                                 |
|o6 = {{0, 1, 2}, {0, 1, 3}, {0, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}}|
|                                                 |
|o6 : List                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+
+-------------------------------------+
|i7 : FF7 = hirzebruchSurface 7;      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i8 : # rays FF7                      |
|                                     |
|o8 = 4                               |
+-------------------------------------+
|i9 : max FF7                         |
|                                     |
|o9 = {{0, 1}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}}|
|                                     |
|o9 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
+------------------------------------------+
|i10 : X = weightedProjectiveSpace {1,2,3};|
+------------------------------------------+
|i11 : # rays X                            |
|                                          |
|o11 = 3                                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i12 : max X                               |
|                                          |
|o12 = {{0, 1}, {0, 2}, {1, 2}}            |
|                                          |
|o12 : List                                |
+------------------------------------------+

In this package, a list corresponding to the maximal cones in the fan is part
of the defining data of a normal toric variety, so this method does no
computation.

See also
========

  * *note making normal toric varieties: making normal toric varieties, --
    information about the basic constructors
  * *note finding attributes and properties: finding attributes and properties,
    -- information about accessing features of a normal toric variety
  * *note rays(NormalToricVariety): rays_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    rays of the associated fan

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note max(NormalToricVariety): max_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    maximal cones in the associated fan
