normalToricVariety(Ring) -- get the associated normal toric variety
*******************************************************************

  * Function: *note normalToricVariety: normalToricVariety_lpList_cmList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        normalToricVariety S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing: normalToricVariety_lpList_cmList_rp, => a *note
        ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ, not used
      * *note MinimalGenerators: normalToricVariety_lpMatrix_rp, => a *note
        Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, not used
      * *note Variable: normalToricVariety_lpList_cmList_rp, => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value x, not used
      * *note WeilToClass: normalToricVariety_lpList_cmList_rp, => a *note
        matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, default value null, not used
  * Outputs:
      * a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 

Description
===========

If a polynomial ring is constructed as the *note total coordinate ring:
ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, of normal toric variety, then this method returns
the associated variety.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : PP3 = toricProjectiveSpace 3;        |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = ring PP3                         |
|                                          |
|o2 = S                                    |
|                                          |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : gens S                               |
|                                          |
|o3 = {x , x , x , x }                     |
|       0   1   2   3                      |
|                                          |
|o3 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : degrees S                            |
|                                          |
|o4 = {{1}, {1}, {1}, {1}}                 |
|                                          |
|o4 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : normalToricVariety S                 |
|                                          |
|o5 = PP3                                  |
|                                          |
|o5 : NormalToricVariety                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert (PP3 === normalToricVariety S)|
+------------------------------------------+
|i7 : variety S                            |
|                                          |
|o7 = PP3                                  |
|                                          |
|o7 : NormalToricVariety                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert (PP3 === variety S)           |
+------------------------------------------+

If the polynomial ring is not constructed from a variety, then this method
produces an error: "no variety associated with ring".

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : S = QQ[x_0..x_2];                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : gens S                                              |
|                                                          |
|o10 = {x , x , x }                                        |
|        0   1   2                                         |
|                                                          |
|o10 : List                                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : degrees S                                           |
|                                                          |
|o11 = {{1}, {1}, {1}}                                     |
|                                                          |
|o11 : List                                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : assert (try (normalToricVariety S; false) else true)|
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : assert instance(variety S, ProjectiveVariety)       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This methods does not determine if a ring could be realized as the total
coordinate ring of a normal toric variety.

See also
========

  * *note working with sheaves: working with sheaves, -- information about
    coherent sheaves and total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
  * *note ring(NormalToricVariety): ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the
    total coordinate ring (a.k.a. Cox ring)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note normalToricVariety(Ring): normalToricVariety_lpRing_rp, -- get the
    associated normal toric variety
