orbits(NormalToricVariety) -- make a hashtable indexing the torus orbits (a.k.a. cones in the fan)
**************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note orbits: orbits_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
  * Usage: 
        orbits X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, whose keys are the
        dimensions of the torus orbits in X and whose values are lists of lists
        of integers indexing the torus orbits

Description
===========

A normal toric variety is a disjoint union of its orbits under the action of
its algebraic torus.  These orbits are in bijection with the cones in the
associated fan.  Each cone is determined by the rays it contains.  In this
package, the rays are ordered and indexed by nonnegative integers: $0, 1,
\dots,n$.  Using this indexing, an orbit or cone corresponds to a sublist of
$\{0,\dots,n\}$; the entries index the rays that generate the cone.

The projective plane has three fixed points and three fixed curves (under the
action of its torus), and projective $3$-space has four fixed points, six fixed
curves, and four divisors.  More generally, the orbits of projective
$(n-1)$-space are enumerated by the $n$-th row of Pascal's triangle.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : O2 = orbits toricProjectiveSpace 2                              |
|                                                                     |
|o1 = HashTable{0 => {{0, 1}, {0, 2}, {1, 2}}}                        |
|               1 => {{0}, {1}, {2}}                                  |
|               2 => {{}}                                             |
|                                                                     |
|o1 : HashTable                                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (#O2#0, #O2#1, #O2#2)                                           |
|                                                                     |
|o2 = (3, 3, 1)                                                       |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : Sequence                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : O3 = orbits toricProjectiveSpace 3                              |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = HashTable{0 => {{0, 1, 2}, {0, 1, 3}, {0, 2, 3}, {1, 2, 3}}    }|
|               1 => {{0, 1}, {0, 2}, {0, 3}, {1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}} |
|               2 => {{0}, {1}, {2}, {3}}                             |
|               3 => {{}}                                             |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : HashTable                                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : apply (4, k -> #O3#k)                                           |
|                                                                     |
|o4 = {4, 6, 4, 1}                                                    |
|                                                                     |
|o4 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : apply (5, k -> # (orbits toricProjectiveSpace 4)#k)             |
|                                                                     |
|o5 = {5, 10, 10, 5, 1}                                               |
|                                                                     |
|o5 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : apply (6, k -> # (orbits toricProjectiveSpace 5)#k)             |
|                                                                     |
|o6 = {6, 15, 20, 15, 6, 1}                                           |
|                                                                     |
|o6 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

Here is a non-simplicial example.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : X = normalToricVariety (id_(ZZ^3) | -id_(ZZ^3));                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert not isSimplicial X                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : OX = orbits X                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = HashTable{0 => {{0, 1, 2, 3}, {0, 1, 4, 5}, {0, 2, 4, 6}, {1, 3, 5, 7}, |
|               1 => {{0, 1}, {0, 2}, {0, 4}, {1, 3}, {1, 5}, {2, 3}, {2, 6}, |
|               2 => {{0}, {1}, {2}, {3}, {4}, {5}, {6}, {7}}                 |
|               3 => {{}}                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : HashTable                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{2, 3, 6, 7}, {4, 5, 6, 7}}            }                                     |
|{3, 7}, {4, 5}, {4, 6}, {5, 7}, {6, 7}}                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : apply (1+dim X, k -> #OX#k)                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = {6, 12, 8, 1}                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The following degenerate example has no fixed points.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : U = normalToricVariety ({{4,-1,0},{0,1,0}},{{0,1}});|
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : assert isDegenerate U                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : OU = orbits U                                       |
|                                                          |
|o13 = HashTable{0 => {}        }                          |
|                1 => {{0, 1}}                             |
|                2 => {{0}, {1}}                           |
|                3 => {{}}                                 |
|                                                          |
|o13 : HashTable                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : apply (4, k -> #OU#k)                               |
|                                                          |
|o14 = {0, 1, 2, 1}                                        |
|                                                          |
|o14 : List                                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : assert (#OU#0 == 0)                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

To avoid repeating a computation, the package caches the result in the *note
CacheTable: (Macaulay2Doc)CacheTable, of the normal toric variety.

See also
========

  * *note finding attributes and properties: finding attributes and properties,
    -- information about accessing features of a normal toric variety
  * *note rays(NormalToricVariety): rays_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- get the
    rays of the associated fan
  * *note orbits(NormalToricVariety,ZZ): orbits_lpNormalToricVariety_cmZZ_rp,
    -- get a list of the torus orbits (a.k.a. cones in the fan) of a given
    dimension

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note orbits(NormalToricVariety): orbits_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make a
    hashtable indexing the torus orbits (a.k.a. cones in the fan)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

