pullback(ToricMap,CoherentSheaf) -- make the pullback of a coherent sheaf under a toric map
*******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note pullback: (Macaulay2Doc)pullback,
  * Usage: 
        F' = pullback(f, F)
        M' = pullback(f, M)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, where the target is smooth
      * F, a *note coherent sheaf: (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,, on the target of
        f or module representing such a coherent sheaf
  * Outputs:
      * F', a *note coherent sheaf: (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,, the pullback of
        F under f, or the module M' representing such a sheaf

Description
===========

The category of coherent *note sheaves: sheaf_lpNormalToricVariety_cmModule_rp,
on a normal toric variety is equivalent to the quotient category of finitely
generated modules over the *note total coordinate ring:
ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, by the full subcategory of torsion modules with
respect to the *note irrelevant ideal: ideal_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,. In
particular, each finitely generated module over the total coordinate ring
corresponds to coherent sheaf on the normal toric variety and every coherent
sheaf arises in this manner. For more information, see Subsection 5.3 in
Cox-Little-Schenck.

A toric morphism $f : X \to Y$ where $Y$ is smooth *note induces:
inducedMap_lpToricMap_rp, a map $g : S \to R$ from total coordinate ring $S$ of
$Y$ to the total coordinate ring $R$ of $X$.  Given a coherent sheaf $F$ on $Y$
corresponding to the $S$-module $M$, the pullback of $F$ along $f$ is the
coherent sheaf corresponding to the $R$-module $M ** g$.  For more information,
see Tomasz Mańdziuk's "Cox rings and algebraic maps", Mathematische Nachrichten
292 (2019) 389-401, arXiv:1703.04794 (see https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.04794 ).
This method returns the sheaf (or module) corresponding to the pullback along
the toric map.

As first example, we compute the pullback of the *note cotangent sheaf:
(Varieties)cotangentSheaf, on the *note projective plane:
toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp, to the first *note Hirzebruch surface:
hirzebruchSurface_lpZZ_rp,.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = hirzebruchSurface 1;                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Y = toricProjectiveSpace 2;                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(Y, X, matrix{{1,0},{0,-1}})                 |
|                                                         |
|o3 = | 1 0  |                                            |
|     | 0 -1 |                                            |
|                                                         |
|o3 : ToricMap Y <--- X                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Omega = cotangentSheaf Y                            |
|                                                         |
|o4 = cokernel {2} | x_2  |                               |
|              {2} | x_0  |                               |
|              {2} | -x_1 |                               |
|                                                         |
|                                         3               |
|o4 : coherent sheaf on Y, quotient of OO  (-2)           |
|                                        Y                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = pullback(f, Omega)                              |
|                                                         |
|o5 = cokernel {0, 2} | x_3     |                         |
|              {0, 2} | x_1x_2  |                         |
|              {0, 2} | -x_0x_1 |                         |
|                                                         |
|                                         3               |
|o5 : coherent sheaf on X, quotient of OO   (0, -2)       |
|                                        X                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : (R = ring X, S = ring Y);                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : inducedMap f                                        |
|                                                         |
|o7 = map (R, S, {x x , x x , x })                        |
|                  1 2   0 1   3                          |
|                                                         |
|o7 : RingMap R <-- S                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : presentation module Omega                           |
|                                                         |
|o8 = {2} | x_2  |                                        |
|     {2} | x_0  |                                        |
|     {2} | -x_1 |                                        |
|                                                         |
|             3      1                                    |
|o8 : Matrix S  <-- S                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : presentation module F                               |
|                                                         |
|o9 = {0, 2} | x_3     |                                  |
|     {0, 2} | x_1x_2  |                                  |
|     {0, 2} | -x_0x_1 |                                  |
|                                                         |
|             3      1                                    |
|o9 : Matrix R  <-- R                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert (isWellDefined f and isHomogeneous module F)|
+---------------------------------------------------------+

For toric divisors, the operations of pullback and taking the associated sheaf
OO commute.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : D = Y_0 + 2*Y_1 + 3*Y_2                             |
|                                                          |
|o11 = Y  + 2*Y  + 3*Y                                     |
|       0      1      2                                    |
|                                                          |
|o11 : ToricDivisor on Y                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : L = pullback(f, OO D)                               |
|                                                          |
|         1                                                |
|o12 = OO   (0, 6)                                         |
|        X                                                 |
|                                                          |
|o12 : coherent sheaf on X, free of rank 1                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : D' = pullback(f, D)                                 |
|                                                          |
|o13 = 2*X  + 3*X  + X  + 3*X                              |
|         0      1    2      3                             |
|                                                          |
|o13 : ToricDivisor on X                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : OO D'                                               |
|                                                          |
|         1                                                |
|o14 = OO   (0, 6)                                         |
|        X                                                 |
|                                                          |
|o14 : coherent sheaf on X, free of rank 1                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : assert (isWellDefined f and L === OO pullback(f, D))|
+----------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This method assumes that the target is smooth. One may verify this by using
*note isSmooth(NormalToricVariety): isSmooth_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,.

See also
========

  * *note working with toric maps: working with toric maps, -- information
    about toric maps and the induced operations
  * *note working with sheaves: working with sheaves, -- information about
    coherent sheaves and total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
  * *note inducedMap(ToricMap): inducedMap_lpToricMap_rp, -- make the induced
    map between total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
  * *note OO ToricDivisor: OO ToricDivisor, -- make the associated rank-one
    reflexive sheaf
  * *note pullback(ToricMap,ToricDivisor):
    pullback_lpToricMap_cmToricDivisor_rp, -- make the pullback of a Cartier
    divisor under a toric map

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note pullback(ToricMap,CoherentSheaf):
    pullback_lpToricMap_cmCoherentSheaf_rp, -- make the pullback of a coherent
    sheaf under a toric map
  * "pullback(ToricMap,Module)"
