pullback(ToricMap,ToricDivisor) -- make the pullback of a Cartier divisor under a toric map
*******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note pullback: (Macaulay2Doc)pullback,
  * Usage: 
        pullback(f, D)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, 
      * D, a *note toric divisor: ToricDivisor,, on the target of f that is
        Cartier
  * Outputs:
      * a *note toric divisor: ToricDivisor,, the pullback of the divisor D
        under the map f

Description
===========

Torus-invariant Cartier divisors pullback under a toric map by composing the
toric map with the support function of the divisor. For more information, see
Proposition 6.2.7 in Cox-Little-Schenck's Toric Varieties.

As a first example, we consider the *note projection: NormalToricVariety ^
Array, from a *note product: NormalToricVariety _st_st NormalToricVariety, of
two *note projective lines: toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp, onto the first
factor.  The pullback of a point is just a fibre in the product.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = toricProjectiveSpace 1;                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = P ** P;                                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = X^[0]                                                  |
|                                                                |
|o3 = | 1 0 |                                                    |
|                                                                |
|o3 : ToricMap P <--- X                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : pullback(f, P_0)                                           |
|                                                                |
|o4 = X                                                          |
|      0                                                         |
|                                                                |
|o4 : ToricDivisor on X                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : pullback(f, 2*P_0 - 6*P_1)                                 |
|                                                                |
|o5 = 2*X  - 6*X                                                 |
|        0      1                                                |
|                                                                |
|o5 : ToricDivisor on X                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert (isWellDefined f and f == map(P, X, matrix {{1,0}}))|
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

The next example illustrates that the pullback of a line through the origin in
*note affine plane: affineSpace_lpZZ_rp, under the *note blowup map:
toricBlowup_lpList_cmNormalToricVariety_cmList_rp, is a line together with the
exceptional divisor.

+---------------------------------+
|i7 : A = affineSpace 2, max A    |
|                                 |
|o7 = (A, {{0, 1}})               |
|                                 |
|o7 : Sequence                    |
+---------------------------------+
|i8 : B = toricBlowup({0,1}, A);  |
+---------------------------------+
|i9 : g = B^[]                    |
|                                 |
|o9 = | 1 0 |                     |
|     | 0 1 |                     |
|                                 |
|o9 : ToricMap A <--- B           |
+---------------------------------+
|i10 : pullback(g, A_0)           |
|                                 |
|o10 = B  + B                     |
|       0    2                    |
|                                 |
|o10 : ToricDivisor on B          |
+---------------------------------+
|i11 : pullback(g, -3*A_0 + 7*A_1)|
|                                 |
|o11 = - 3*B  + 7*B  + 4*B        |
|           0      1      2       |
|                                 |
|o11 : ToricDivisor on B          |
+---------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note working with toric maps: working with toric maps, -- information
    about toric maps and the induced operations
  * *note isCartier(ToricDivisor): isCartier_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether a
    torus-invariant Weil divisor is Cartier
  * *note pullback(ToricMap,CoherentSheaf):
    pullback_lpToricMap_cmCoherentSheaf_rp, -- make the pullback of a coherent
    sheaf under a toric map

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note pullback(ToricMap,ToricDivisor):
    pullback_lpToricMap_cmToricDivisor_rp, -- make the pullback of a Cartier
    divisor under a toric map
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

