sheaf(NormalToricVariety,Module) -- make a coherent sheaf
*********************************************************

  * Function: *note sheaf: (Varieties)sheaf,
  * Usage: 
        sheaf (X, M)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note normal toric variety: NormalToricVariety,, 
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a graded module over the
        total coordinate ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note coherent sheaf: (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,, the coherent sheaf
        on X corresponding to M

Description
===========

The category of coherent sheaves on a normal toric variety is equivalent to the
quotient category of finitely generated modules over the *note total coordinate
ring: ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, by the full subcategory of torsion modules
with respect to the *note irrelevant ideal: ideal_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,.  In
particular, each finitely generated module over the total coordinate ring
corresponds to coherent sheaf on the normal toric variety and every coherent
sheaf arises in this manner.  For more information, see Subsection 5.3 in
Cox-Little-Schenck's Toric Varieties.

Free modules correspond to reflexive sheaves.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : PP3 = toricProjectiveSpace 3;            |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = sheaf (PP3, (ring PP3)^{{1},{2},{3}})|
|                                              |
|          1            1            1         |
|o2 = OO    (1) ++ OO    (2) ++ OO    (3)      |
|       PP3          PP3          PP3          |
|                                              |
|o2 : coherent sheaf on PP3, free of rank 3    |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : FF7 = hirzebruchSurface 7;               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G = sheaf (FF7, (ring FF7)^{{1,0},{0,1}})|
|                                              |
|          1                1                  |
|o4 = OO     (1, 0) ++ OO     (0, 1)           |
|       FF7              FF7                   |
|                                              |
|o4 : coherent sheaf on FF7, free of rank 2    |
+----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note working with sheaves: working with sheaves, -- information about
    coherent sheaves and total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
  * *note ring(NormalToricVariety): ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the
    total coordinate ring (a.k.a. Cox ring)
  * *note ideal(NormalToricVariety): ideal_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the
    irrelevant ideal
  * *note sheaf(NormalToricVariety): sheaf_lpNormalToricVariety_cmRing_rp, --
    make a coherent sheaf of rings

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note sheaf(NormalToricVariety,Module):
    sheaf_lpNormalToricVariety_cmModule_rp, -- make a coherent sheaf
