todd(CoherentSheaf) -- compute the Todd class of a coherent sheaf
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note todd: (Schubert2)todd,
  * Usage: 
        todd F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note coherent sheaf: (Varieties)CoherentSheaf,, on a complete
        simplicial normal toric variety
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in the intersection
        ring of the underlying variety

Description
===========

Given a locally-free sheaf $E$ of rank $r$ on a smooth variety such that its
Chern class formally factor as chern $E = \prod_{j=1}^r (1 + \alpha_j)$, we
define its Todd class to be todd $E := \prod_{j=1}^r \alpha_j / [1-
exp(-\alpha_j)]$ written as a polynomial in the elementary symmetric functions
chern $(i, E)$ of the $\alpha_j$.

The first few components of the Todd class are easily related to Chern classes.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X0 = kleinschmidt(4, {1,3,5});                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E0 = cotangentSheaf X0                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = cokernel {2, 0}  | 2x_2x_3 4x_1x_3 5x_0x_3 0     0    2x_1x_2 0         |
|              {-7, 2} | x_4     0       0       0     x_1  0       0         |
|              {-7, 2} | -x_5    0       0       0     0    0       0         |
|              {-5, 2} | 0       x_4     0       x_2   0    0       0         |
|              {-5, 2} | 0       -x_5    0       0     0    0       x_2       |
|              {-4, 2} | 0       0       x_4     0     0    0       0         |
|              {-4, 2} | 0       0       -x_5    0     0    0       0         |
