toricDivisor(Polyhedron) -- make the toric divisor associated to a polyhedron
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note toricDivisor: toricDivisor_lpList_cmNormalToricVariety_rp,
  * Usage: 
        toricDivisor P
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, whose vertices
        are lattice points
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ,
        that determines the coefficient ring of the total coordinate ring of
        the underlying normal toric variety
      * Variable => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value x,
        that specifies the base symbol for the indexed variables in the total
        coordinate ring of the underlying normal toric variety
      * WeilToClass => a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, default value
        null, that specifies the map from the group of torus-invariant Weil
        divisors to the class group of the underlying normal toric variety
  * Outputs:
      * a *note toric divisor: ToricDivisor,, corresponding to the given convex
        lattice polytope on the normal toric variety defined by the inner
        normal fan

Description
===========

A convex lattice polytope corresponds to a pair: the normal toric variety
determined by its normal fan and toric divisor.  The coefficient of the $i$-th
irreducible torus-invariant divisor is determined by the supporting hyperplane
to the polytope whose normal vector is the minimal lattice point on the $i$-th
ray.

Our example demonstrates how different triangles correspond to toric divisors
on the projective plane.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P1 = convexHull matrix{{0,1,0},{0,0,1}};                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D1 = toricDivisor P1                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = D                                                                       |
|      2                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ToricDivisor on normalToricVariety ({{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, -1}}, {{0, 1},|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{0, 2}, {1, 2}})                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = variety D1;                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : D1                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = X                                                                       |
|      2                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : ToricDivisor on X                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : P2 = convexHull matrix{{-1,0,-1},{0,0,1}};                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : D2 = toricDivisor P2                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = D                                                                       |
|      0                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : ToricDivisor on normalToricVariety ({{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, -1}}, {{0, 1},|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{0, 2}, {1, 2}})                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : P3 = convexHull matrix{{0,1,0},{-1,-1,0}};                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : D3 = toricDivisor P3                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = D                                                                       |
