ToricMap -- the class of all torus-equivariant maps between normal toric varieties
**********************************************************************************

Description
===========

Let $X$ and $Y$ be normal toric varieties whose underlying lattices are $N_X$
and $N_Y$ respectively.  A toric map is a morphism $f : X \to Y$ that induces a
morphism of algebraic groups $g : T_X \to T_Y$ such that $f$ is
$T_X$-equivariant with respect to the $T_X$-action on $Y$ induced by $g$.
Every toric map $f : X \to Y$ corresponds to a unique map $f_N : N_X \to N_Y$
between the underlying lattices such that, for every cone $\sigma$ in the fan
of $X$, there is a cone in the fan of $Y$ that contains the image
$f_N(\sigma)$. For details see Theorem 3.3.4 in Cox-Little-Schenck.

To specify a map of normal toric varieties, the target and source normal toric
varieties need to be specified as well as a matrix which maps from $N_X$ to
$N_Y$.

The primary constructor of a toric map is *note
map(NormalToricVariety,NormalToricVariety,Matrix):
map_lpNormalToricVariety_cmNormalToricVariety_cmMatrix_rp,.

See also
========

  * *note working with toric maps: working with toric maps, -- information
    about toric maps and the induced operations
  * *note NormalToricVariety: NormalToricVariety, -- the class of all normal
    toric varieties
  * *note id _ NormalToricVariety: id _us NormalToricVariety, -- make the
    identity map from a NormalToricVariety to itself
  * *note isWellDefined(ToricMap): isWellDefined_lpToricMap_rp, -- whether a
    toric map is well defined

