ToricMap * ToricMap -- make the composition of two toric maps
*************************************************************

  * Operator: *note *: (Macaulay2Doc)_st,
  * Usage: 
        g * f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, a toric map between toric varieties
      * g, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, a toric map between toric varieties
  * Outputs:
      * a *note toric map: ToricMap,, the composition g * f from source f to
        target g

Description
===========

Given two toric maps with the target of first equal to the source of second,
this method returns the composite map from source of the first to target of the
second.

We illustrate this construction with the projection from a *note smooth Fano
Toric threefold: smoothFanoToricVariety_lpZZ_cmZZ_rp, to the first *note
Hirzebruch surface: hirzebruchSurface_lpZZ_rp, and a projection from this
Hirzebruch surface to the *note projective line: toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp,.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = smoothFanoToricVariety(3,14);                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Y = hirzebruchSurface 1;                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(Y, X, matrix{{1,0,0},{0,1,0}})                        |
|                                                                   |
|o3 = | 1 0 0 |                                                     |
|     | 0 1 0 |                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o3 : ToricMap Y <--- X                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert (isWellDefined f and source f === X and target f === Y)|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Z = toricProjectiveSpace 1;                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g = map(Z, Y, matrix{{1, 0}})                                 |
|                                                                   |
|o6 = | 1 0 |                                                       |
|                                                                   |
|o6 : ToricMap Z <--- Y                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert (isWellDefined g and source g === Y and target g === Z)|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : h = g * f                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o8 = | 1 0 0 |                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o8 : ToricMap Z <--- X                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert (isWellDefined h and source h === X and target h === Z)|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : X = hirzebruchSurface 1;                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

Composing *note diagonal maps: diagonalToricMap, and canonical *note
projections: NormalToricVariety ^ Array, yields *note identity maps: id _us
NormalToricVariety,.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : X2 = X ** X;                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : delta = diagonalToricMap X                                |
|                                                                |
|o12 = | 1 0 |                                                   |
|      | 0 1 |                                                   |
|      | 1 0 |                                                   |
|      | 0 1 |                                                   |
|                                                                |
|o12 : ToricMap X2 <--- X                                        |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : assert (X2^[0] * delta == id_X and X2^[1] * delta == id_X)|
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

