weilDivisorGroup(ToricMap) -- make the induced map between groups of Weil divisors
**********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note weilDivisorGroup: weilDivisorGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
  * Usage: 
        weilDivisorGroup f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note toric map: ToricMap,, with a smooth target
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, representing the map of abelian
        groups between the corresponding groups of torus-invariant Weil
        divisors

Description
===========

Given a toric map $f : X \to Y$ where $Y$ a smooth toric variety, this method
returns the induced map of abelian groups from the group of torus-invariant
Weil divisors on $Y$ to the group of torus-invariant Weil divisors on $X$.  For
arbitrary normal toric varieties, the *note weilDivisorGroup:
weilDivisorGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, is not a functor.  However, *note
weilDivisorGroup: weilDivisorGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, is a contravariant
functor on the category of *note smooth: isSmooth_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,
normal toric varieties.

We illustrate this method on the projection from the first *note Hirzebruch
surface: hirzebruchSurface_lpZZ_rp, to the *note projective line:
toricProjectiveSpace_lpZZ_rp,.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = hirzebruchSurface 1;                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Y = toricProjectiveSpace 1;                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(Y, X, matrix {{1, 0}})                                 |
|                                                                    |
|o3 = | 1 0 |                                                        |
|                                                                    |
|o3 : ToricMap Y <--- X                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f' = weilDivisorGroup f                                        |
|                                                                    |
|o4 = | 0 1 |                                                        |
|     | 0 0 |                                                        |
|     | 1 0 |                                                        |
|     | 0 0 |                                                        |
|                                                                    |
|              4       2                                             |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert (isWellDefined f and source f' == weilDivisorGroup Y and|
|         target f' == weilDivisorGroup X)                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

The next example gives the induced map from the group of torus-invariant Weil
divisors on the projective plane to the group of torus-invariant Weil divisors
on the first Hirzebruch surface.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Z = toricProjectiveSpace 2;                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : g = map(Z, X, matrix {{1, 0}, {0, -1}})                        |
|                                                                    |
|o7 = | 1 0  |                                                       |
|     | 0 -1 |                                                       |
|                                                                    |
|o7 : ToricMap Z <--- X                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : g' = weilDivisorGroup g                                        |
|                                                                    |
|o8 = | 0 1 0 |                                                      |
|     | 1 1 0 |                                                      |
|     | 1 0 0 |                                                      |
|     | 0 0 1 |                                                      |
|                                                                    |
|              4       3                                             |
|o8 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert (isWellDefined g and source g' == weilDivisorGroup Z and|
|         target g' == weilDivisorGroup X)                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------+

The induced map between the groups of torus-invariant Weil divisors is
compatible with the induced map between the *note class groups:
classGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : g'' = classGroup g                                   |
|                                                           |
|o10 = | 0 |                                                |
|      | 1 |                                                |
|                                                           |
|               2       1                                   |
|o10 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : assert(g'' * fromWDivToCl Z  == fromWDivToCl X  * g')|
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note working with toric maps: working with toric maps, -- information
    about toric maps and the induced operations
  * *note weilDivisorGroup(NormalToricVariety):
    weilDivisorGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the group of
    torus-invariant Weil divisors
  * *note classGroup(ToricMap): classGroup_lpToricMap_rp, -- make the induced
    map between class groups
  * *note cartierDivisorGroup(NormalToricVariety):
    cartierDivisorGroup_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- compute the group of
    torus-invariant Cartier divisors
  * *note pullback(ToricMap,ToricDivisor):
    pullback_lpToricMap_cmToricDivisor_rp, -- make the pullback of a Cartier
    divisor under a toric map

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note weilDivisorGroup(ToricMap): weilDivisorGroup_lpToricMap_rp, -- make
    the induced map between groups of Weil divisors
