working with divisors -- information about toric divisors and their related groups
**********************************************************************************

The following methods allows one to make and manipulate torus-invariant Weil
divisors on a normal toric variety.

Operations on toric divisors
============================

  * *note ToricDivisor: ToricDivisor, -- the class of all torus-invariant Weil
    divisors
  * *note toricDivisor(List,NormalToricVariety):
    toricDivisor_lpList_cmNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make a torus-invariant Weil
    divisor
  * *note toricDivisor(NormalToricVariety):
    toricDivisor_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the canonical divisor
  * *note toricDivisor(Polyhedron): toricDivisor_lpPolyhedron_rp, -- make the
    toric divisor associated to a polyhedron
  * *note smallAmpleToricDivisor(ZZ,ZZ): smallAmpleToricDivisor_lpZZ_cmZZ_rp,
    -- get a very ample toric divisor from the database
  * *note NormalToricVariety _ ZZ: NormalToricVariety _us ZZ, -- make an
    irreducible torus-invariant divisor
  * *note normalToricVariety(ToricDivisor): variety_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- get
    the underlying normal toric variety
  * *note expression(ToricDivisor): expression_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- get the
    expression used to format for printing
  * *note support(ToricDivisor): support_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- make the list of
    irreducible divisors with nonzero coefficients
  * *note entries(ToricDivisor): entries_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- get the list of
    coefficients
  * *note ToricDivisor + ToricDivisor: divisor arithmetic, -- perform
    arithmetic on toric divisors
  * *note OO ToricDivisor: OO ToricDivisor, -- make the associated rank-one
    reflexive sheaf
  * *note isEffective(ToricDivisor): isEffective_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether
    a torus-invariant Weil divisor is effective
  * *note isCartier(ToricDivisor): isCartier_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether a
    torus-invariant Weil divisor is Cartier
  * *note isQQCartier(ToricDivisor): isQQCartier_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether
    a torus-invariant Weil divisor is QQ-Cartier
  * *note isNef(ToricDivisor): isNef_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether a
    torus-invariant Weil divisor is nef
  * *note nefGenerators(NormalToricVariety):
    nefGenerators_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- compute generators of the nef
    cone
  * *note isAmple(ToricDivisor): isAmple_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether a
    torus-invariant Weil divisor is ample
  * *note isVeryAmple(ToricDivisor): isVeryAmple_lpToricDivisor_rp, -- whether
