working with sheaves -- information about coherent sheaves and total coordinate rings (a.k.a. Cox rings)
********************************************************************************************************

David A. Cox (see http://www3.amherst.edu/~dacox/ ) introduced the total
coordinate ring $S$ of a normal toric variety $X$ and the irrelevant ideal $B$.
The polynomial ring $S$ has one variable for each ray in the associated fan and
a natural grading by the class group.  The monomial ideal $B$ encodes the
maximal cones.  The following results of Cox indicate the significance of the
pair $(S,B)$.

  * The variety X is a good categorical quotient of Spec(S) -  V(B) by a
    suitable group action.
  * The category of coherent sheaves on X is equivalent to the quotient of the
    category of finitely generated graded S-modules by the full subcategory of
    B-torsion modules.

In particular, we may represent any coherent sheaf on $X$ by giving a finitely
generated graded $S$-module.

The following methods allow one to make and manipulate coherent sheaves on
normal toric varieties.

Sheaf-theoretic methods
=======================

  * *note ring(NormalToricVariety): ring_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the
    total coordinate ring (a.k.a. Cox ring)
  * *note ideal(NormalToricVariety): ideal_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the
    irrelevant ideal
  * *note sheaf(NormalToricVariety,Ring): sheaf_lpNormalToricVariety_cmRing_rp,
    -- make a coherent sheaf of rings
  * *note sheaf(NormalToricVariety,Module):
    sheaf_lpNormalToricVariety_cmModule_rp, -- make a coherent sheaf
  * *note OO ToricDivisor: OO ToricDivisor, -- make the associated rank-one
    reflexive sheaf
  * *note cotangentSheaf(NormalToricVariety):
    cotangentSheaf_lpNormalToricVariety_rp, -- make the sheaf of Zariski
    1-forms
  * *note HH^ZZ(NormalToricVariety,CoherentSheaf):
    HH^ZZ_lpNormalToricVariety_cmCoherentSheaf_rp, -- compute the cohomology of
    a coherent sheaf
  * *note intersectionRing(NormalToricVariety): Chow ring, -- make the rational
    Chow ring
